{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 30, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a member of the House of Tripoli a noble family of the Kingdom of Jerusalem. He was born around 1152 AD and was the son of Bohemond III of Tripoli and his wife Orgueilleuse of Antioch. Raymond III's early life and family background are not well documented.\n\n* **Family Background** * \nRaymond III was the son of Bohemond III of Tripoli and Orgueilleuse of Antioch. His father was the Count of Tripoli and his mother was a member of the House of Antioch a noble family of the Kingdom of Jerusalem. Raymond III's family was part of the nobility of the Kingdom of Jerusalem and held significant power and influence in the region.\n\nRaymond III married a woman named Eschiva of Bures. The marriage is documented in the Itinerarium Peregrinorum et de Gestis Regis Ricardi which is a medieval manuscript that provides information about the history of the Kingdom of Jerusalem. The Itinerarium Peregrinorum et de Gestis Regis Ricardi is a valuable source of information about Raymond III's life and marriage.\n\n* **Reign as Count of Tripoli** *\nRaymond III succeeded his father Bohemond III as the Count of Tripoli. He reigned as the Count of Tripoli from around 1184 to 1187. During his reign as Count of Tripoli Raymond III faced significant challenges including the threat of Muslim armies. The Muslim armies were a major threat to the Kingdom of Jerusalem and the nobility of the region.\n\nRaymond III was also involved in a conflict with the Kingdom of Jerusalem over the County of Tripoli. The conflict was over the rights and privileges of the County of Tripoli. Raymond III's involvement in the conflict highlights the complex and often contentious relationships between the nobility of the Kingdom of Jerusalem.\n\nRaymond III died in 1187. His death was likely the result of the conflict with the Muslim armies. The death of Raymond III marked the end of the House of Tripoli as the ruling family of the County of Tripoli.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.014390614}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -0.00016938205}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -0.0010648064}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.1300828}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -3.349725e-05}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -0.00021371941}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -6.651657e-05}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.015882885}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.34376433}, {"token": " member", "logprob": -0.5870414}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -4.3748852e-05}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.00829915}, {"token": " House", "logprob": -0.27775657}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -5.483477e-05}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -1.0981891}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -0.00077872945}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -1.1372362}, {"token": " noble", "logprob": -0.27681324}, {"token": " family", "logprob": -0.03713842}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -1.0338436}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.46114662}, {"token": " Kingdom", "logprob": -0.337068}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -8.034383e-05}, {"token": " Jerusalem", "logprob": -0.005299686}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -0.3950912}, {"token": " He", "logprob": -0.12322249}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.095497996}, {"token": " born", "logprob": -1.0503899}, {"token": " around", "logprob": -0.7855154}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -0.011871993}, {"token": "115", "logprob": -0.6415355}, {"token": "2", "logprob": -0.33467975}, {"token": " AD", "logprob": -1.1334248}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.868488}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.32947585}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.034879383}, {"token": " son", "logprob": -0.15988341}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.0004650465}, {"token": " Boh", "logprob": -0.53565425}, {"token": "em", "logprob": -7.998623e-05}, {"token": "ond", "logprob": -0.0036291708}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -0.038862642}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -1.5831043}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -1.2